      ],
      "margin_number": 1,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "ἣ Your first relative pronoun: feminine because it goes with Lysistrata, nominative because it is the subject of the verb in its clause.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 6,
      "bbox": [
        191,
        544,
        869,
        578
      ],
      "margin_number": 3,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "καταλύσασαι What part of the verb is this? Women are the subject of the sentence.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 7,
      "bbox": [
        191,
        583,
        905,
        617
      ],
      "margin_number": 5,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "ἴδοιμι From ὁράω. The second aorist is εἶδον, the aorist stem is ἰδ- and this is the aorist optative.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 8,
      "bbox": [
        191,
        621,
        841,
        656
      ],
      "margin_number": 6,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "6–7 καὶ Κλεονίκη ... κἀμοί = καὶ ἐμοί; what does καί mean in both these phrases?",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 9,
      "bbox": [
        191,
        660,
        892,
        693
      ],
      "margin_number": 8,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "οὖσαι What part of the verb? It's a participle, and we are still talking about women.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 10,
      "bbox": [
        191,
        697,
        886,
        751
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "οὗ What gender, what case? Why? See GE p. 216, #216. Note that in the nominative case m.s., f.s., and pl. the relative pronoun has an accent, whereas the article has none.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": 3,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
